\title{levyfit: maximum likelihood estimation for degradation processes}
\description{
\code{levyfit} estimates the parameters of stochastic degradation models from one
or several degradation trajectories observed at regular or irregular
inspection times. All the parameters are estimated by maximum likelihood
(maximum likelihood estimator, MLE). The help page of each function gives
the model, the likelihood and how the estimator is computed.
}
\section{Functions of the package}{

Estimation of the parameters:\tabular{llll}{
   Function \tab Process \tab Parameters \tab Computation \cr
   \code{\link[=wiener_mle]{wiener_mle()}} \tab Wiener with drift \tab \code{mu}, \code{sigma2}, \code{s2} \tab closed form \cr
   \code{\link[=gamma_mle]{gamma_mle()}} \tab gamma \tab shape \code{a}, rate \code{b} \tab root of one equation \cr
   \code{\link[=ig_mle]{ig_mle()}} \tab inverse Gaussian \tab \code{mu}, \code{eta}, \code{eta_unbiased} \tab closed form \cr
   \code{\link[=vg_mle]{vg_mle()}} \tab variance-gamma \tab \code{theta}, \code{sigma}, \code{nu} \tab EM, then L-BFGS-B \cr
   \code{\link[=meixner_mle]{meixner_mle()}} \tab Meixner \tab \code{a}, \code{b}, \code{d}, \code{m} \tab profile likelihood \cr
}


\code{s2} and \code{eta_unbiased} are the unbiased versions of \code{sigma2} and \code{eta}.
Every estimation function returns the point estimates and, with
\code{ci = TRUE}, asymptotic confidence intervals. \code{\link[=increments_data]{increments_data()}} gives the
data by their increments
instead of their levels.

Inspection times following a chosen pattern, and simulated trajectories
to try the estimators, are given by the package \code{DegradSim}
(\code{DegradSim::inspection_times()} and its simulation functions).
